  "objective": "Fix RECHECK-03 durable-flush/index/maintenance bottlenecks, verify locally before bounded expansion.",
  "startingState": "Existing preparation fixes, bilingual documents and reports preserved. No retained 100k fixture resumed; no commit/push.",
  "changes": {
    "ST-79": "Optional portable IWorkspaceMutationBatch; one bounded FIFO for mixed journal range/metadata callbacks, including Overwrite and Open. Caller retains native input; handles and success follow durability. 64 callback/chunk units and 16MiB staging; oversized single callbacks retain existing split barriers, unsupported stores retain fallback. Only mutating leaders with multiple open handles yield until a 100us monotonic deadline, without holding mutation/journal gates or timer sleep. FIFO completion watermarks and post-flush diagnostic accounting remain ordered.",
    "ST-80": "ExtentList.Truncate saves its node only when a private extent root changes; entry/base-length/timestamp commits and zero-fill semantics remain.",
    "ST-81": "Shadow-tail Replay uses existing bounded node/name/namespace/change-index batches. Full catchup/root/native/ownership proofs and durable rotation remain; no accepted ACK is published by private shadow replay.",
    "ST-82": "Local literal/runtime contracts, native buffer/ACK/failure/drain/cleanup/large-transfer tests, small packing recovery and cache/read guards; all intermediate/unfavorable measurements retained."
  },
